id: ce_oem_switchdev_ports
_summary: Enumerate switchdev fabric ports
_description:
    Generates the list of netdevs exposing phys_switch_id (switch fabric
    ports). Ports listed under reserved_ports in the setup config JSON
    (checkbox config SWITCHDEV_SETUP_CONFIG, e.g. the management/infra
    uplink) are marked reserved: True so destructive templates exclude
    them. Schema: data/switchdev-setup.schema.json.
plugin: resource
category_id: com.canonical.plainbox::ethernet
estimated_duration: 2
environ: SWITCHDEV_SETUP_CONFIG
command: switchdev_test.py resource

id: ce-oem-switchdev/port-count
_summary: Check the expected number of switchdev fabric ports enumerate
_description:
    Counts netdevs with phys_switch_id and compares against the
    expected_ports key of the setup config JSON (e.g. 29 = 24 copper +
    4 SFP+ + management on a Tactical-1000 class device).
plugin: shell
user: root
category_id: com.canonical.plainbox::ethernet
estimated_duration: 5
environ: SWITCHDEV_SETUP_CONFIG
imports: from com.canonical.plainbox import manifest
requires: manifest.has_switchdev_test_setup == 'True'
command: switchdev_test.py port-count

unit: template
template-resource: ce_oem_switchdev_ports
template-filter: ce_oem_switchdev_ports.reserved == 'False'
template-unit: job
template-id: ce-oem-switchdev/link-flap
_template-summary: Admin link flap recovery on each switchdev fabric port
id: ce-oem-switchdev/link-flap-{interface}
_summary: Admin link flap recovery on fabric port {interface}
_description:
    Repeatedly admin-down/up the port and verify the link recovers each
    time. Ports without link at start (empty ports) pass as skip. Reserved
    infra ports are excluded by the template filter.
plugin: shell
user: root
category_id: com.canonical.plainbox::ethernet
estimated_duration: 180
environ: SWITCHDEV_SETUP_CONFIG
imports: from com.canonical.plainbox import manifest
requires: manifest.has_switchdev_test_setup == 'True'
command: switchdev_test.py link-flap --interface {interface}

id: ce-oem-switchdev/vlan-config-drift
_summary: Frozen bridge VLAN table matches the saved baseline
_description:
    The permanent test setup freezes the bridge/VLAN layout in the boot config.
    This job diffs the live `bridge vlan` table against the baseline JSON
    at the vlan_baseline path of the setup config JSON. Create the baseline
    once on a known-good test setup with:
    switchdev_test.py vlan-drift --config <setup config> --save
plugin: shell
user: root
category_id: com.canonical.plainbox::ethernet
estimated_duration: 5
environ: SWITCHDEV_SETUP_CONFIG
imports: from com.canonical.plainbox import manifest
requires: manifest.has_switchdev_test_setup == 'True'
command: switchdev_test.py vlan-drift

id: ce-oem-switchdev/chain-offload-proof
_summary: Chain traffic is forwarded by the switch ASIC (offload proof)
_description:
    Sends iperf3 UDP between the chain-entry SVI and the chain-exit SVI
    (moved into a netns) in BOTH directions so traffic traverses the
    permanently wired loop-cable chain each way, then asserts: traffic
    arrived (loss below threshold per direction), hardware-offloaded FDB
    entries exist, and a mid-chain fabric port actually carried the packets.
    UDP is deliberate: a fixed offered rate keeps loss assertable, while
    TCP congestion control would slow down and hide path problems.
    Chain endpoints come from the chain object of the setup config JSON.
    Requires iperf3 on the device and the permanent test setup VLAN plan.
plugin: shell
user: root
category_id: com.canonical.plainbox::ethernet
estimated_duration: 60
environ: SWITCHDEV_SETUP_CONFIG
imports: from com.canonical.plainbox import manifest
requires: manifest.has_switchdev_test_setup == 'True'
command: switchdev_test.py offload-proof

id: ce-oem-switchdev/stp-loop-protection
_summary: STP contains the pre-provisioned loop and fails over
_description:
    Brings up the permanently cabled same-VLAN fixture pair (admin-down by
    default, named by stp_fixture_ports in the setup config JSON) with
    kernel classic (802.1D) STP enabled: one port must go blocking (loop
    contained), and admin-downing the forwarding port must promote the
    blocked one. Restores ports down and the bridge STP state afterwards.
    RSTP via mstpd is a planned upgrade of this job.
plugin: shell
user: root
category_id: com.canonical.plainbox::ethernet
estimated_duration: 300
environ: SWITCHDEV_SETUP_CONFIG
imports: from com.canonical.plainbox import manifest
requires: manifest.has_switchdev_stp_fixture == 'True'
command: switchdev_test.py stp-fixture

id: ce-oem-switchdev/l3-offload-probe
_summary: Report whether L3 routes are hardware-offloaded (informational)
_description:
    Informational probe: reports whether any kernel route carries the
    offload flag. On devices whose driver lacks L3 offload this documents
    the CPU-path routing status per release; it never fails the run.
    Runs only when switchdev fabric ports exist.
plugin: shell
user: root
category_id: com.canonical.plainbox::ethernet
estimated_duration: 5
requires: ce_oem_switchdev_ports.switch_id != ''
command: switchdev_test.py l3-offload-probe

id: ce-oem-switchdev/vrf-probe
_summary: Report whether VRF creation is supported (informational)
_description:
    Informational probe: tries to create and delete a VRF device and
    reports driver/kernel support status; it never fails the run.
    Runs only when switchdev fabric ports exist.
plugin: shell
user: root
category_id: com.canonical.plainbox::ethernet
estimated_duration: 5
requires: ce_oem_switchdev_ports.switch_id != ''
command: switchdev_test.py vrf-probe
